# Branding: the backend's brand is DEPLOY-PINNED (its group limits / e-mail identity don't
# live-switch), and it is what every other service acquires its archives from (GET /branding/…).
# Archives (`*.tar.gz`) are found recursively, without any configuration, under two roots:
#   deployment/configurations     next to the running process — in the container that is
#                                 /app/deployment/configurations, where a branded build bakes its
#                                 archive and where docker-compose mounts the brand sources in dev.
#   ../deployment/configurations  the same directory seen from a repo checkout, because `npm run dev`
#                                 runs from backend/.
# Both are always tried (@ocelot-social/branding discover.DEFAULT_ROOTS) and one that does not exist
# costs a single failed readdir, which is what lets ONE default be correct in the image and in a
# checkout. So for dev, only the pin below is needed. The matching archive is discovered and read at
# startup (nodemon restarts on src changes; restart to pick up config edits). The backend only READS
# these; it has no sync cache, unlike the webapp. Unpinned and without a DEFAULT marker → vanilla.
#
# OCELOT_BRANDING_ASSETS_DIR REPLACES both locations above with an ORDERED search path (`:`-separated;
# an earlier root shadows a later one per brand id) — a mounted volume, and later the bucket users
# upload their own archives into.
# OCELOT_BRANDING_ASSETS_DIR=
# OCELOT_ACTIVE_BRANDING=

NEO4J_URI=bolt://localhost:7687
